--- attribute axis: parameters that `equals` treats as interchangeable stay exact ---
attr Tuple(UInt8,UInt8)/Tuple(Bool,UInt8) declines	1
attr Tuple(UInt8,UInt8)/Tuple(Bool,UInt8)	1
--- an actual NULL in a nullable set element (the cross-type cast rewrites it to the nested default) ---
null-elem NOT IN stays exact	1
null-elem NOT IN	1
null-elem identity keeps pruning	1
null-elem identity	1	1
--- the lossy conversion path, not the element type, is what forfeits exactness ---
lossy mixed array NOT has declines	0
lossy mixed array NOT has	0	1
lossy cross-type array NOT has declines	0
lossy cross-type array NOT has	0	1
safe identity actual NULL keeps pruning	1
safe identity actual NULL IN keeps pruning	1
safe identity actual NULL	1	1
safe cross-type NOT IN keeps pruning	1
safe cross-type NOT IN	1
safe cross-type array NOT has keeps pruning	1
safe cross-type array NOT has	1
safe nullable tuple keeps pruning	1
safe nullable tuple	1
